/* Jacob's Pillow Dance Interactive — where a person or a work can be watched
 * in the Pillow's own archive.
 *
 * Filled by tools/find-pillow.mjs, which searches their site by name and keeps
 * only what a human-checkable slug confirms. This pass read the same catalogue
 * through the site's own public search index, whose records carry the
 * choreographer and the performing company as separate fields — so a work here
 * was kept only where that choreographer is one of the work's makers on this
 * map, and a person only where the page is about them, their company, or a
 * dance they made. Nothing was kept on a title alone.
 *
 * These are LINKS, never embeds, and that is deliberate. The Pillow serves its
 * video as a signed Vimeo file whose token expires, so an embed would break
 * silently — the worst failure for an archive reference. The underlying Vimeo
 * id is technically embeddable, but lifting the video out of their site strips
 * the attribution from an archive that publishes this for nothing. A link is
 * the honest way to use somebody else's collection.
 *
 * One rule the matching pass works under, and one entry it cost. A link may
 * only point at the thing the node IS. The atlas's Jardin aux Lilas node is
 * the 1962 Folkwang revival; the Pillow's film is the National Ballet of
 * Canada in 1953 — the same choreography, a different staging nine years
 * earlier — so it is not linked. This is the same judgement footage-overrides
 * .json already makes for YouTube: an excerpt of a work may stand for it, and
 * a different production may not.
 */
