      "note": "The big one: 350,100 items in 398 containers, 590 linear feet, spanning 1896 to 2003, call number ML31.G727, bought with Doris Duke Charitable Foundation money in 1998. The finding aid names the highlights — a Music Inventory covering 73 of her works with holograph scores by Copland, Barber, Horst, Hovhaness, El-Dabh, Dello Joio, Hindemith, Menotti, Schuman, Riegger and Starer, and piano rehearsal scores that often carry her choreographic notes in the margins; and scrapbooks from 1926 to 1976 that include Germany's official invitation to the 1936 Olympics together with Graham's carbon copy of her answer. The PDF is free and is the map to everything the atlas already cites as 'the Library of Congress listing'.",
