      "note": "An hour on the German Ausdruckstanz of 1905–1933 — Wigman's own generation and her own subject — put together from surviving film of the period and the testimony of people who had been in the room. It is a film about the movement rather than about her alone, so treat it as context; but it is the fullest German-language film survey of the world she made, and the second part, 'Einsame Streiter', continues it. In German. The copy is a re-upload of a Bayerischer Rundfunk broadcast, not the producer's own.",
