      "note": "There is no book about Bolm. This exhibit essay from the library that holds his papers is the nearest thing: the Maryinsky, organising Pavlova's first tour outside Russia, the Ballets Russes American tours he took over when Fokine and Nijinsky could not travel, Krazy Kat, the Danse Macabre film, Chicago Allied Arts, the San Francisco Opera Ballet in 1932, and the pupils — Cyd Charisse, Janet Collins, Lester Horton, Ruth Page. It closes on his own words from a 1937 radio programme about what American ballet would become.",
