      "url": "https://synchronousobjects.osu.edu/",
      "note": "Twenty 'objects' that take the counterpoint of One Flat Thing, reproduced (2000) apart and rebuild it as data — alignment annotations, cue scores, movement-density maps. Built by Forsythe with Maria Palazzi and Norah Zuniga Shaw at Ohio State's ACCAD. The Flash interactives died with Flash on 31 December 2021; the archive site that replaced them keeps video of all twenty objects, the interface documentation and the process notes, and says plainly that market-driven software obsolescence is what killed the original.",
