      "note": "The catalogue Forsythe keeps of his own installations, films and exhibitions, and the place his essay 'Choreographic Objects' is published in full — the argument that choreography is 'the method of deriving methods', that choreography and dancing are two different practices, and that the principles can live in an object with no body in it. Read the essay page first; the exhibition and film indexes are how you find which object is which.",
