      "url": "http://scores.motionbank.org/",
      "note": "Forsythe founded Motion Bank inside The Forsythe Company in 2010 to see whether a choreographer's thinking could be published as a digital score. The four scores that came out of it are here and still run — Deborah Hay's Using the Sky, Jonathan Burrows and Matteo Fargion's Seven Duets, Bebe Miller and Thomas Hauert's Two, and a door back to Synchronous Objects. The scores are of other choreographers; what they show is Forsythe's method of turning practice into something readable.",
