      "note": "Alessandra Ascarelli's entry — the fullest scholarly life in his own language, free to read: born in his mother's dressing room at the Teatro Apollo, thrown out of school in Florence for hurling an inkwell, second maître de ballet at the Mariinsky, the first Carabosse and the first Bluebird. It closes by arguing that Beaumont's codification, in stripping the method to principles and step sequences, cut away the theatrical seeing that held it together. Full bibliography of the early sources at the foot.",
