      "note": "A finding aid rather than a book, and the only institutional life of her anywhere: née Goldsmith, an MA from Sarah Lawrence, the Cunningham company 1958 to 1963, married to Robert Dunn and divorced in 1966, then the Judith Dunn/Bill Dixon Company, and teaching at Brandeis, Sarah Lawrence, the Cunningham studio, Teachers College and Bennington. The collection is mostly film and video of her classes and improvised performances. On-site only.",
