      "url": "https://books.openedition.org/septentrion/69003",
      "note": "Philippe Guisgand wrote his doctorate on her and this is the book of it: 342 pages working out what actually defines her choreographic style, from the movement outward — composition assimilated bodily rather than imposed, and the close hold on music. Free to read in full on OpenEdition Books since June 2020. In French; there is no English equivalent at this depth.",
      "src": "Presses universitaires du Septentrion, Villeneuve d'Ascq, 2008, collection 'Esthétique et sciences des arts', ISBN 978-2-7574-0029-6; open access on OpenEdition Books, DOI 10.4000/books.septentrion.69003"
