   "src": "Elizabeth McPherson, 'Martha Hill: Supporting the Creative Work of José Limón', Congress on Research in Dance Conference Proceedings vol. 39 S1 (Cambridge University Press, 2013): 'The Connecticut College School of the Dance/American Dance Festival began in 1948, with Hill and Ruth Bloomer as co-directors; it continued the ideas behind the Bennington School of the Dance.' Duke University Libraries, American Dance Festival records, Martha Hill series (archives.lib.duke.edu/catalog/adfadfrecords_aspace_a0260ca1dd79db4993e8b1e9357ac44d): 'In 1953, she became \"advisory\" co-director of the festival, leaving Ruth Bloomer as director.'"
