   "about": "From introduction, p. v: “In New Dance Ms. Humphrey explores the relationship of the individual and the group within society and their eventual unity and ideal state of harmony. A work of absolute dance which John Martin described as ‘comparable to a symphony,’ the dance celebrates the fulfillment of the individual in his relation to a group…New Dance was an affirmation of faith in a possible democratic society, in which the individual could develop his own capabilities in harmonious relationship with, and to the benefit of his fellow.”",
