/* Where each person came from, and where they took it.
 *
 * Four fields, not one "nationality", because a single label says "American"
 * for Asadata Dafora and for Michio Ito and those are not the same sentence.
 * Dafora was born in Freetown into a family that had returned to Sierra Leone
 * after enslavement in Nova Scotia; Ito was held by the United States in four
 * internment camps and deported. Where a border has moved since, the modern
 * country is the field and the historical entity is in the note.
 *
 *   born    the modern country, for grouping
 *   place   the town or city, where the record gives one
 *   worked  countries they worked in that are NOT the one they were born in —
 *           the crossing, which is the part worth reading
 *   note    what the label cannot carry
 *   src     who says so, head only: the passes quote the books at length and
 *           the books stay on the machine that holds them
 *
 * 376 of the map's people, across 52 countries. 182 of them worked
 * somewhere they were not born, which is the same argument this map makes
 * about traditions, one axis over.
 *
 * Generated from research/dance-origins by build-data.cjs. Do not edit.
 */
