  "src": "The Noguchi Museum, Biography, noguchi.org/isamu-noguchi/biography/biography — 'Noguchi was born in Los Angeles, but moved to Japan with his mother at the age of two and lived there until the age of thirteen. In the summer of 1918, Noguchi returned alone to the United States to attend high school in Rolling Prairie and then La Porte, Indiana'; The Noguchi Museum exhibition 'Self-Interned, 1942: Noguchi in Poston War Relocation Center' for the voluntary internment and the quotation; English Wikipedia, 'Isamu Noguchi' infobox birth_place Los Angeles, California"
