  "note": "El Arte de Vivir el Flamenco reproduces her passport for the birth record and describes the Amayas as a Gitano family of artists — the same household as Carmen, Paco, Leonor, María and Antonio. She danced inside her sister's touring company, and ExpoFlamenco names her in a company photograph taken in Argentina in 1940 or 1941; the American years belong to that company. The map's paragraph flags her AncientFaces genealogy date as sitting oddly against the family's other dates, and it does: the research file records that pass having found 1886, which would have made her older than her father.",
  "src": "El Arte de Vivir el Flamenco, 'ANTONIA AMAYA' — 'ANTONIA AMAYA AMAYA... nació en Barcelona el día 16 de septiembre del año de 1923. Hija de El Chino, llamado José Amaya Amaya y de Micaela Amaya Moreno, según nos revela su pasaporte', and 'lo lleva en su cuerpo dentro de la sangre de raza gitana de una amplia familia de artista'; ExpoFlamenco, 'Sabicas' father was Carmen Amaya's guitarist (I)' — 'Carmen Amaya looking at her sisters Antonia and Leonor... The photograph was taken in Argentina, in 1940 or 1941'"
