  "note": "An American born in Japan: her parents were United States Navy during the Occupation. Wikipedia says she grew up in Yokohama and also that she moved to the United States at three, which do not sit together comfortably, and no source I could open names the city she was actually born in — hence the empty born_place. Her butoh route runs the opposite way to most on this list: she met Min Tanaka in New York in 1984 and joined Maijuku there, and only then went to Japan to study with Tanaka and with Ohno Kazuo and Ohno Yoshito; Decay of the Angel was commissioned by the Japan-U.S. Creative Artist Commission and premiered in Tokyo in 2000.",
  "src": "en.wikipedia, Maureen Fleming — 'Fleming was born in Japan and grew up in Yokohama, the daughter of parents in the United States Navy... She moved with her parents to the United States when she was three years old'; maureenfleming.com About page — 'Maureen Fleming was born in Japan'; Fraleigh, Butoh (2010) — 'She was born in Japan, the daughter of an American Navy lieutenant.'"
