  "place": "Triana, Seville, Andalusia",
  "note": "Birth year contested. For 1954: es.wikipedia's lede, 'n. Sevilla, 1954', and El Arte de Vivir el Flamenco. For 21 October 1958: andalucia.org (Junta de Andalucía), ExpoFlamenco, and Vida Flamenca — which is this map's own cited source and says 1958. es.wikipedia's own infobox carries the 1958 date against its 1954 lede. On the family, es.wikipedia and the Bienal de Sevilla biography both say she was born 'de cuna gitana, en el barrio de Triana en una familia de artistas, en el Tejado del Moro', daughter of the bailaor José Carrasco 'El Sordo' and Cipriana Salazar Heredia.",
